    {
      "title": "TEST PROCEDURE",
      "items": [
        {
          "type": "textarea",
          "key": "test_procedure",
          "label": "Test Procedure",
          "default": "The test procedure was in accordance with <Standard name>.\n\nPower Line:\n\nThe EUT was tested in the CRF test site with a GRP. The EUT was placed on a 0.1 m insulation support on the GRP. The cables between the coupling and decoupling devices and the EUT was kept as short as possible, and it was neither bundled nor wrapped and the cable was kept 30mm above the reference ground plane. The power supply to the EUT was fed through a CDN which is bonded to the GRP. The RF power from the signal source was amplified and fed through the RF input port of the CDN and superimposed on the power lines of the EUT with reference to ground plane.\n\nSignal Line:\n\nThe EUT was tested in the CRF test site with a ground reference plane. The EUT was placed on a 0.1 m insulation support on the GRP. The RF power from the signal source was amplified and fed through the RF port of the EM clamp and superimposed on the signal lines of the EUT with reference to ground plane.\n\nThe RF voltage was amplitude modulated to 80% depth with 1 kHz sine wave in the frequency range as per standard. During the test, performance of the EUT was monitored as per the criteria specified in standard."
        }
      ]
    },
